stateDiagram-v2
    %% Current Org Auth ceremony lifecycle; transition guards and evidence are in the inventory.
    state "issued (status_id 10)" as issued
    state "admitted (status_id 20)" as admitted
    state "evidence_recorded (status_id 30)" as evidence
    state "replaced (status_id 40)" as replaced
    state "revoked (status_id 90)" as revoked
    state "completed (status_id 91)" as completed
    state "cancelled_before_progress (status_id 92)" as cancelled_before
    state "cancelled_after_progress (status_id 93)" as cancelled_after

    [*] --> issued: issue!
    [*] --> admitted: rotate_and_admit! without predecessor
    issued --> admitted: admit!
    admitted --> evidence: record_authentication_evidence!
    issued --> replaced: rotate_and_admit! replaces predecessor
    admitted --> replaced: rotate_and_admit! replaces predecessor
    evidence --> replaced: rotate_and_admit! replaces predecessor
    issued --> revoked: revoke!
    admitted --> revoked: revoke!
    evidence --> revoked: revoke!
    issued --> issued: rotate! same row
    admitted --> admitted: rotate! same row
    evidence --> evidence: rotate! same row
    admitted --> completed: complete!
    evidence --> completed: complete!
    admitted --> cancelled_before: cancel!
    evidence --> cancelled_after: cancel!
    issued --> [*]: retention after expiry and the final binding reference
    admitted --> [*]: retention after expiry and the final binding reference
    evidence --> [*]: retention after expiry and the final binding reference
    replaced --> [*]: retention after revocation and the final binding reference
    revoked --> [*]: retention after revocation and the final binding reference
    completed --> [*]: retention after completion and the final binding reference
    cancelled_before --> [*]: retention after cancellation and the final binding reference
    cancelled_after --> [*]: retention after cancellation and the final binding reference

    note right of issued
        operator_auth_ceremony_session_statuses is an id-only reference table.
        status_id is NOT NULL and is written only by AuthCeremonySession.
        TTL expiry makes active? false without a state write.
        rotate! changes SID facts but keeps the lifecycle status.
        The binding collector deletes an expired row only after its final
        binding reference is gone and the status-specific retention boundary
        has elapsed. It does not write a replacement status.
    end note

    note right of replaced
        rotate_and_admit! changes a nonterminal predecessor to replaced
        and creates the admitted row in one OP transaction. An already
        terminal predecessor keeps its original terminal state.
    end note

    note right of cancelled_before
        Parent Cancel may end an admitted or evidence-recorded ceremony while
        its OIDC parent remains unfinalized. Org has no public Switch route.
    end note
end
